# Medarx artifacts
#
# `/capture/` is anchored to the repository root on purpose. The unanchored
# `capture/` matched `infra/capture/` as well — so the agreement check and the
# capture script, which are source, sat inside an ignore rule meant for the
# directory a capture *writes to*, and `git add infra/capture` added nothing.
/capture/
*.pcap
# The committed capture readback under `backend/tests/fixtures/capture/` is
# deliberately *not* matched by either rule: the hex readback of a capture this
# host actually took is the evidence the agreement check is tested against, and
# a check proven only against a string someone typed is not proven. The
# readbacks are named `*.pcap.txt` so `*.pcap` leaves them alone.
evals/reports/
evals/synthetic_phi/eval_results.json

# The handoff is a working document, not a tracked one. `backend/README.md` is
# the only document this repository tracks, and a `git add -A` that swept this
# in would quietly change that.
/HANDOFF.md
